+# Design — Your Reinvention Roadmap
+
+## Art direction
+
+Calm, assured editorial graphics with a navigation-system motif. The visual world is deliberate rather than futuristic: precise rules, simple waypoints, clear labels, and generous space.
+
+## Palette
+
+- Deep navy `#0a1e2f` and navy `#0d2437` establish the field.
+- Gold `#eaab2d` identifies decisions, active waypoints, and the final commitment.
+- Blue `#3393d6` carries the route and supporting information.
+- Paper `#ffffff`, cultured `#f6f6f9`, and muted video `#5f6f96` support readable hierarchy.
+
+## Typography
+
+Use Proxima Nova with the system sans-serif fallback. Headlines are 72–104px at weight 900; supporting copy is 40–48px; labels are 22px uppercase with wide tracking. No essential text falls below the token minimum.
+
+## Layout
+
+Maintain 120px frame padding and reserve the lower 120px. A persistent top-left module label and top-right progress counter frame each scene. Content occupies the center-left; diagrams and map elements balance the right side. Cards use 12px radii and 2px borders.
+
+## Motion
+
+All animation is controlled by one paused GSAP timeline. Text enters with 24px of vertical travel and opacity; rules draw left to right; the route draws through four waypoints. Entrances settle within 1.2 seconds and content exits in 0.3 seconds. The final arrow extends during the closing second. There are no infinite animations.
+
+## Accessibility
+
+High-contrast paper text sits on navy. Visual labels reinforce, but never replace, spoken meaning. Motion is short, directional, and free of flashing.
+
